00:00:04.749 --> 00:00:07.990 align:start position:0%
july the 1st  2020 and one of the last big protests in  hong kong  a gathering held in defiance of social  distancing rules  and a sweeping new national security law  the same law  under which tong yin kit has now been  convicted  it was the day disobedience accelerated  these images capturing the moment tong  drove his motorcycle  towards a group of policemen attached to  his machine  a banner proclaiming liberate hong kong  revolution of our times  that was a cry heard constantly during  the unrest  tong had pleaded not guilty to both  charges on which he was convicted  his trial happened without a jury  instead the verdict  was delivered by a panel of three judges  appointed by hong kong's chief executive  carrie lam  the reasons the judge gave for their  verdict runs to more than 60 pages  but in essence they say that tong fully  understood  that the words on his protest banner  equated to a call  for independence and that the slogan was  capable of inciting others  he'll be sentenced at a later date but  faces a life term  more than 120 people have so far been  charged under the national security  legislation  including the publisher jimmy ly who was  also in court on tuesday  like tong he too faces spending the rest  of his life  in jail adrian brown al jazeera hong  kong
 

